  "body": "## What it changes\n\n- Renames `patterns/azure/database_private_access/` to `patterns/azure/postgresql_private_access/`.\n- Renames the PostgreSQL delegated-subnet example from `examples/azure/database/postgresql/private_access/basic/` to `examples/azure/database/postgresql/private_access/delegated_subnet/`.\n- Renames the PostgreSQL delegated-subnet diagram assets from `*_basic_*` to `*_delegated_subnet_*`.\n- Updates README/docs references to the new pattern and example paths.\n- Updates the PostgreSQL private-access scenario README so `delegated_subnet` is the first available variant and `private_endpoint` is explicitly planned.\n\n## Scope discipline\n\nNo Terraform logic was changed in this PR. The only Terraform file content change is the example module source path and the pattern guardrail error message name after the directory rename.\n\n## Validation\n\nRan successfully:\n\n```text\ntofu fmt -recursive\ntofu init -backend=false   # patterns/azure/postgresql_private_access\ntofu validate              # patterns/azure/postgresql_private_access\ntofu init -backend=false   # examples/azure/database/postgresql/private_access/delegated_subnet\ntofu validate              # examples/azure/database/postgresql/private_access/delegated_subnet\ntofu plan -refresh=false   # examples/azure/database/postgresql/private_access/delegated_subnet, 17 to add / 0 to change / 0 to destroy\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nNotes:\n\n- `tofu fmt -recursive` reported format-only changes in unrelated OCI files; those were reverted before commit to keep this PR rename-only.\n- `tofu plan -refresh=false` was run with the active Azure subscription/tenant and a valid temporary SSH public key supplied only as process-local variables.\n- `tofu apply` / `tofu destroy` were not rerun for this rename-only PR; the underlying PostgreSQL delegated-subnet implementation was already applied, validated through Bastion, and destroyed in PR #6.\n- Generated `.terraform/`, `.terraform.lock.hcl`, and state artifacts were removed before commit.\n\n## Deferred to later PRs\n\n- Azure SQL private-access pattern using Private Endpoint\n- Azure MySQL private-access pattern using delegated subnet\n- Azure Cosmos DB private-access pattern using Private Endpoint\n- PostgreSQL Private Endpoint variant for `postgresql_private_access`\n- Secure variants, additional engines, app-to-data, multi-spoke, cross-region DR/replication, governance, and private blueprint-tier topologies",
